  <content>
    <procedure>
      <commonInfo>
        <title>Job description</title>
        <para>This procedure gives the information regarding the removal and installation
of rivnuts.</para>
      </commonInfo>
      <preliminaryRqmts>
        <reqCondGroup>
          <noConds />
        </reqCondGroup>
        <reqSupportEquips>
          <supportEquipDescrGroup>
            <supportEquipDescr>
              <name>Standard Mechanician Tools</name>
              <toolRef toolNumber="No specific" manufacturerCodeValue="Commercially available" />
              <reqQuantity unitOfMeasure="As Required" />
            </supportEquipDescr>
          </supportEquipDescrGroup>
        </reqSupportEquips>
        <reqSupplies>
          <noSupplies />
        </reqSupplies>
        <reqSpares>
          <noSpares />
        </reqSpares>
        <reqSafety>
          <safetyRqmts>
            <note>
              <notePara>Only approved personnel must do the maintenance to the component.</notePara>
            </note>
          </safetyRqmts>
        </reqSafety>
      </preliminaryRqmts>
      <mainProcedure>
        <proceduralStep>
          <title>Procedure</title>
          <proceduralStep>
            <title>Removal procedure of rivnuts with cylinder and countersunk head shapes</title>
            <para>Refer to <internalRef internalRefId="B7772S11MONA25301201003663AC_fig-05" /> Rivnut Removal and Installation</para>
            <proceduralStep>
              <caution>
                <warningAndCautionPara>MUST BE CAREFUL NOT TO MAKE THE EXISTING HOLE BIGGER.</warningAndCautionPara>
              </caution>
              <para>With a drill bit of 6.1 mm (0.24 in) (for rivnut thread size 6/32 or 8/32) and 7.1 mm (0.28 in) for rivnut thread size 10/32, drill slowly by making circular movements to cut and remove the rivnut head.</para>
            </proceduralStep>
          </proceduralStep>
          <proceduralStep>
            <title>Installation procedure of rivnuts with cylinder and countersunk head shapes</title>
            <para>Refer to <internalRef internalRefId="B7772S11MONA25301201003663AC_fig-05" /> Rivnut Removal and Installation</para>
            <proceduralStep>
              <caution>
                <warningAndCautionPara>EXAMINE THAT THE CORRECT SIZE PULL-UP STUD IS INSTALLED
IN THE HEADER DEPENDING UPON THE RIVNUT THREAD SIZE.</warningAndCautionPara>
              </caution>
              <para>Place new rivnut head-first on the pull-up stud of the manual tool and screw till the anvil. Follow supplier manual for more instructions.</para>
              <note>
                <notePara>The necessary pull-up stud(s) must be procured from the tool supplier depending upon the rivnut thread size.</notePara>
              </note>
              <note>
                <notePara>If the pull-up stud necessary to be changed, follow the steps given in the tool supplier manual.</notePara>
              </note>
            </proceduralStep>
            <proceduralStep>
              <para>The rivnut head must be in touch with the anvil and the pull-up stud must be flush with the rivnut open end. Follow supplier manual if adjustment is necessary.</para>
            </proceduralStep>
            <proceduralStep>
              <para>Place the tool with the rivnut in the hole and press tightly the handle refer to <internalRef internalRefId="B7772S11MONA25301201003663AC_tab-001" />.</para>
            </proceduralStep>
            <proceduralStep>
              <para>Upon releasing the handle, the tool will be released from the rivnut. Follow supplier manual for more instructions.</para>
              <?pb ?>
